.TH tine-export-query 1  "query " 
.SH NAME
tine\-export\-query \- Publish result pages of a query into published\-queries/. Sheets keep plain row outlines, as in other command\-line exports
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtine export query\fR [\fB\-\-query\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-page\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-comments\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIGRAPH\fR> [\fI((UUID))\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Publish result pages of a query into published\-queries/. Sheets keep plain row outlines, as in other command\-line exports
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-query\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Inline argument of a query macro: Logseq simple or advanced, as decided by the shared parser
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable diagnostic logging for the desktop app
.TP
\fB\-\-page\fR \fI<PAGE>\fR
First query on this page, in document order (parents before children; embeds are not followed)
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Output name; required for \-\-query, otherwise the title or Query UUID/PAGE
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace an existing output, keeping the previous export in recovery
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-comments\fR
Leave comment threads out of this export
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIGRAPH\fR>

.TP
[\fI((UUID))\fR]
Persisted block UUID, bare or wrapped as ((UUID)); quote parentheses in the shell
